    "feedback": "Approve. The candidate is the iteration 5 design (best raced, 417.25) with one field changed: controller.line_loss goes from last_direction to search_right. Geometry is unchanged: sensors at x = -0.05 to 0.05 (0.025 spacing), y = 0.07, sensor_size 0.012. The sensor_size 0.016 change from iteration 6 is not repeated, because it scored lower (350.07) and cut the oval finish rate to 0.9, s-bend progress to 0.29 and slalom progress to 0.12. The controller gains (kp 1.5, ki 0.5, kd 0.4, base_speed 1.2) are also unchanged, since kd 0.4 is what fixed the oval in iteration 3 (max_error 0.043).\n\nThe reason to test line_loss now is the iteration 3 to 6 pattern. Slalom has shown exactly 1 line-loss event per run at a fixed point, with progress stuck near 0.19. Sensor position and footprint changes did not move that point. So the loss is more likely a recovery-behaviour problem than a geometry limit. Hypothesis (a): a fixed left-steering search recovers the line better than last_direction at the first-bend overshoot. Note that line_loss affects the oval as well (0.75 events per run in iteration 5), so the oval must be checked too.\n\nRead the result in this order. (1) If slalom progress rises above 0.2 and oval finish stays at 0.8 or more, keep search_right and move on to other levers. (2) If slalom progress is unchanged or falls, the drift is probably to the right, so test search_left next. (3) If the oval finish rate drops below 0.8, revert to last_direction and keep the iteration 5 result as the baseline. Measurements wanted: per-track progress, finish rate, line_loss_events, and the side the robot leaves the line on each track.",
    "requested_changes": [
      "If slalom progress is unchanged or falls with controller.line_loss search_right, change controller.line_loss to search_left (keeping geometry at iteration 5 values), since slalom loss has been fixed at 1 per run across iterations 3 to 6 and the side of loss is still unknown.",
